  "DISCLOSURE_1_THE_QUOTA_PROPERTY": {
    "statement": "The threshold is a percentile of the very distribution the test is applied to. Choosing the 99th therefore FIXES the exclusion rate at 1% of measured-gap pairs before any data is looked at. The data decides WHICH pairs are excluded; it does not decide HOW MANY. The number 632 is not a property of viewing behaviour and does not mark any feature of the gap distribution -- there is no elbow, no shoulder, no mode near it. It is the level that delivers a pre-chosen quota. That is the price of a rate that is true as stated, and it is disclosed rather than argued away.",
