  "DISCLOSURE_2_THE_INERTNESS": {
    "statement": "The measured-gap test -- the part the threshold governs -- does a small minority of the liveness filter's work. At the proposed 99th percentile it excludes 1,276 pairs while decisions/0036 \u00a72.3's two evidence-absence edge cases exclude 22,496. The threshold accounts for 5.37% of liveness exclusions and the edge-case rulings for 94.63%. A reader must not take the threshold to be doing work it is not doing: the liveness filter is overwhelmingly two rulings about ABSENT evidence, not a measurement of silence.",
